$ah — run Anthill (.ah) source from texts[]

SUMMARY
  Parses and executes .ah program text from texts[], using the same session
  and UI callback as the parent run. Returns the nested program's output
  bundle (images[], videos[], prompts[], etc.).

SYNTAX
  $ah
  $ah(entry='gen_clip')

INPUT
  texts[] — required; one or more links containing .ah source (e.g. output of $code).
  Other input arrays are not passed into the nested run (entry starts with empty arrays).

OUTPUT
  The final ArrayBundle from running the nested script (replaces the input bundle).
  Writes script.ah and nested_run.json under the op dir for inspection.

ARGUMENTS
  entry= — run this @instruction instead of the script's `run @…` target.

BEHAVIOR
  Always runs in-process (nested Runtime + ActionCallback).
  Nested work is stored under <op_dir>/nested/; returned bundle links are
  reparented to the parent session so later steps can read them.
  Nested @instructions and $externals emit the same action_start/finish/error
  callbacks as the main app flow (UI resolves previews from each op's session).

  Optional fence stripping: if texts[] starts with ``` or ```ah, the fence is removed.
  LLM-style escapes (\\n, \\\", \\t) in texts[] are expanded before parse ($ah only).

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_AH=1 — placeholder texts[] output, no nested execution.

EXAMPLE
  @ah_code: $file('_lang_desc', source_path=True) -> $ah_code_examples(folder='examples', per_usecase=20) -> $code -> $ah
  Create a script that builds an image clip about cats.

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — reads texts[], not prompts[].
